[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sifu-Hotman/More-Mod-Patches-for-Expanded-Materials-Masonry/main/Media/Badge_MMMas.png[/img]

A bunch of unofficial mod patches for [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3662913084]Expanded Materials - Masonry[/url]. I did my best to match that author's conventions: concrete (EM_CementMix) takes 25% of the Steel cost on heavy conventional, civil and structural buildings, nothing else changes.

[h1]Coverage[/h1]
24 buildings across 5 mods:
[list]
[*][b]Combat Extended Armory[/b] (12): every manned emplacement and turret, from the 12-pounder bombard to the Vickers and the SPG-9.
[*][b]Combat Extended Guns[/b] (1): 105mm howitzer.
[*][b]Alpha Biomes[/b] (5): propane turret, both magma-thermal generators, core sample drill, bone drill.
[*][b]Vanilla Quests Expanded - The Generator[/b] (5): all five ARC generators.
[*][b]Vanilla Quests Expanded - Drone Factory[/b] (1): drone autofactory (concrete pad under the chassis, factor 2.5 like EMMas does for factory machinery).
[/list]
Full per-building list on [url=https://github.com/Sifu-Hotman/More-Mod-Patches-for-Expanded-Materials-Masonry#coverage]GitHub[/url].

[h1]Requires / load order[/h1]
Argonic Core and Expanded Materials - Masonry. Load this [b]after[/b] Expanded Materials - Masonry and [b]after Combat Extended[/b]. If you also run [url=https://github.com/Sifu-Hotman/More-Mod-Patches-for-Expanded-Materials-Metals]More Mod Patches for Expanded Materials - Metals[/url], this one goes first:

Argonic Core -> Expanded Materials - Masonry -> this mod -> Expanded Materials - Metals -> Metals mod patches

[h1]FAQ[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]CE compatible?[/b] Yes. Load this after CE.
[*][b]Add or remove mid-save?[/b] Yep.
[*][b]Balance?[/b] Same rule EMMas applies to its own buildings, nothing more.
[*][b]A mod you'd like covered?[/b] Open an issue on GitHub with the building names.
[/list]

[h1]AI[/h1]
This mod was engineered with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude Code). Researching the compatibility interfaces of every patched mod would have been insurmountable without it. Development followed a standard process driven and scrutinized by me: explore, design, build, test, fix, review, test again over many rounds. I have manually reviewed and verified everything in this mod. If you have unconstructive feedback about the use of AI, please keep it outside this community space. Thank you.

